From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: a drag that ended before it began does not end
 every later one

WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging notes a drag as begun
(drag_security_info_.OnDragInitiated) and then gives it up if the button is
already up, or the pointer outside the view: it told the renderer
(SystemDragEnded) but not the security info, which held the drag as begun for
good. Every later drag of that tab then returned at the top of the function
without a word to the renderer, which waits in its drag and takes no press:
the page was dead to clicks (not to scrolling) until loaded again, and again
at the next press that moved. A link clicked with the pointer moving, as a
head moves it in the room, is such a drag. Now the security info is told; the
early return tells the renderer too; and a drag that ended with nothing taken
does not wait for an exit of this view that may not come (0026's case from
its other side).
---
 .../browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc       | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
index 4f45307..f36dc4f 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
@@ -1228,6 +1228,10 @@ void WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging(
       static_cast<RenderWidgetHostImpl*>(source_rfh.GetRenderWidgetHost());
   // Disallow reentrant drag which could be an attempt to exploit drag state.
   if (drag_security_info_.did_initiate()) {
+    // Spatiand: the renderer waits to hear that the drag it asked for is over
+    // and takes no press until it does: told so here too, where it was left
+    // waiting (the page then heard no click until it was loaded again).
+    web_contents_->SystemDragEnded(source_rwh);
     return;
   }
   if (!aura::client::GetDragDropClient(root_window)) {
@@ -1297,6 +1301,11 @@ void WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging(
          !env->is_touch_down()) ||
         (event_info.source == ui::mojom::DragEventSource::kMouse &&
          !env->IsMouseButtonDown())) {
+      // Spatiand: this drag is over before it began (the button came up while
+      // the page was asking: a link clicked with the pointer moving, as a
+      // head moves it). Said to the security info too, or it held the drag as
+      // begun for good and every later drag of the page was dropped above.
+      drag_security_info_.OnDragEnded();
       web_contents_->SystemDragEnded(source_rwh);
       return;
     }
@@ -1311,6 +1320,7 @@ void WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging(
     // visible.
     if (!content_native_view->GetBoundsInScreen().Contains(trusted_location) ||
         !content_native_view->IsVisible()) {
+      drag_security_info_.OnDragEnded();  // Spatiand: as above.
       web_contents_->SystemDragEnded(source_rwh);
       return;
     }
@@ -1339,6 +1349,12 @@ void WebContentsViewAura::StartDragging(
   // If drag is still in progress that means we haven't received drop targeting
   // callback yet. So we have to make sure to delay calling EndDrag until drop
   // is done.
+  // Spatiand: a drag that ended with nothing taken has no drop of its own to
+  // wait for: its end is said now even if this view still holds a drag as
+  // being over it (an exit that did not come), instead of never.
+  if (drag_in_progress_ && result_op == DragOperation::kNone) {
+    OnDragExited();
+  }
   if (!drag_in_progress_) {
     EndDrag(std::move(source_rwh_weak_ptr), result_op);
   } else {
-- 
